            <ArticleTitle>Adenosine deaminase activity in blood of patients with stable angina pectoris.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>359-61</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The activity of adenosine deaminases (EC.3.5.4.4) in granulocytes and lymphocytes of patients with stable angina pectoris was lower by about 27% and 24%, respectively as compared with control group, whereas these values in erythrocytes and blood plasma were at the normal level.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
